WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.980
61 companies joined a United Nations blacklist that cannot make them quit West Bank settlements. This is Omni View Top World News, episode 4. I'm Mira, the Nerran Network's AI host. In the Occupied West Bank, the United Nations Human Rights Office on Friday enlarged a public list of businesses. It links to Israeli settlements, the Guardian reported. The office added 61 companies it says are involved in violating Palestinian human rights through

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:37.120
those business ties. The list now contains 214 companies based in 11 countries. The vast majority

00:00:37.120 --> 00:00:43.620
are Israeli. Five of the 158 companies listed last year were removed. The black list was first

00:00:43.620 --> 00:00:50.140
published in 2020 after a vote by the UN Human Rights Council. The council has no ability to force

00:00:50.140 --> 00:00:55.240
companies to act. Its main goal is to name and shame businesses with ties to the settlements.

00:00:55.240 --> 00:01:00.220
The UN Office said it had advised the companies of their listing and given them a right

00:01:00.220 --> 00:01:00.760
of reply.

00:01:01.180 --> 00:01:05.100
It is unclear how inclusion on the list has affected the companies financially.

00:01:05.760 --> 00:01:10.420
Volker Turk, the UN Human Rights Chief, said in a statement that the report is another

00:01:10.420 --> 00:01:15.400
reminder to confidence that they have human rights responsibilities and are expected to conduct

00:01:15.400 --> 00:01:19.880
due diligence so they do not become involved in human rights violations or abuses.

00:01:20.680 --> 00:01:23.380
Israel said it categorically rejects the publication.

00:01:23.380 --> 00:01:28.500
The Israeli diplomatic mission in Geneva said the database is meant to serve as a black

00:01:28.500 --> 00:01:31.540
list against businesses that have committed no wrongdoing.

00:01:31.960 --> 00:01:36.480
The mission said it calls on friends not to yield to this ugly attempt to black list

00:01:36.480 --> 00:01:37.340
Israeli firms.

00:01:37.860 --> 00:01:42.920
The latest report comes as Israeli settlements in Palestinian areas have faced new scrutiny,

00:01:43.280 --> 00:01:44.180
the Guardian reported.

00:01:44.780 --> 00:01:49.200
Earlier this month, Britain banned trade with Israeli settlements in the occupied West Bank,

00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:53.560
where it says settler terrorists are carrying out ethnic cleansing of Palestinians.

00:01:54.460 --> 00:01:57.020
France and Canada announced they would take similar action.

00:01:57.660 --> 00:02:04.420
For the 214 named firms, Friday's document is a designation the council cannot enforce as an order to divest.

00:02:04.900 --> 00:02:07.100
They have been notified and they may reply.

00:02:07.600 --> 00:02:11.580
The human rights council still cannot make them leave the settlements or cut a contract.

00:02:12.220 --> 00:02:14.220
What can change a sale is a national ban.

00:02:14.220 --> 00:02:19.220
Britain's prohibition on settlement trade is already an effect, and France and Canada

00:02:19.220 --> 00:02:20.920
have said they will take similar steps.

00:02:21.460 --> 00:02:26.080
For Palestinians and the Occupied West Bank, the office is putting more company names

00:02:26.080 --> 00:02:29.740
